 "entry": "volve_3d",
 "kind": "REAL_FIELD_EXCERPT_FOR_THE_3D_VIEW",
 "field": "Volve, Norwegian North Sea (blocks 15/9), operated by Statoil/Equinor, decommissioned 2016",
 "publisher": "Equinor ASA, with the former Volve licence partners ExxonMobil Exploration and Production Norway AS and Bayerngas Norge AS",
 "license": "Equinor's 'Terms and conditions for licence to data - Volve' (2020): use, copy and adapt for non-commercial and commercial purposes; Equinor and the former partners attributed and a notice referring to the terms included when shared; the licensed material may not be sold; no use that suggests endorsement. (The 2018 release carried CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; Equinor replaced it.)",
 "license_url": "https://cdn.equinor.com/files/h61q9gi9/global/de6532f6134b9a953f6c41bac47a0c055a3712d3.pdf?equinor-hrs-terms-and-conditions-for-licence-to-data-volve.pdf=",
 "attribution": "Contains data from the Volve field released by Equinor ASA and the former Volve licence partners ExxonMobil Exploration and Production Norway AS and Bayerngas Norge AS.",
 "access": "The release itself (Equinor's data village) was not reachable from the build machine; the files were taken from public GitHub copies, each at a pinned commit, hashed as fetched. Byte identity with the original release is not claimed; the checks below are what tie the copies to the field and to each other.",
 "crs": "ED50 / UTM zone 31N (International 1924 ellipsoid), metres - as delivered; depths below mean sea level, positive down",
 "checks": [
  "the slot eastings and northings of 15/9-F-1 C and 15/9-F-11 B, unprojected on ED50 zone 31N, land 0.02 m and 0.09 m from the latitudes and longitudes in those wells' own LAS headers (and about 148 m away if read as WGS84) - the frame is ED50 zone 31N",
  "the minimum-curvature path computed from each trajectory file's measured depths, inclinations and azimuths reproduces the TVD and displacements written in the file to under a centimetre (15/9-F-4, -F-5, -F-10)",
  "the paths land on Equinor's own formation picks, which carry eastings, northings and depths, to under 0.3 m",
  "the horizons are in depth below sea level (they tie to the picks' TVDSS, not to their two-way times): median miss 2 to 6 m by surface at the 23-28 wells picked for each, larger at a few wells the interpretation did not honour (listed per surface in the scene)"
 ],
 "findings": [
  "15/9-F-4's definitive survey (Baker Hughes, gyro, 2016) says true north; Equinor's picks on F-4 agree with it to 0.1 m read as grid azimuths and miss by up to 14 m with the 0.95 degree convergence applied. The scene reads it as grid and says so.",
  "15/9-F-4's 2016 survey stamps every station with one time (a resurvey): it is not a record of drilling and is not replayed.",
  "The seabed horizon in the same copy is two blocks, the second in two-way time; it is not used.",
  "No copy of the real-time drilling logs from the wells' drilling (2007-2009) was found under an open licence; the 2016 logs that are copied are plug-and-abandonment work with the string near surface. The Volve replay therefore follows the survey stations' own times."
 ],
